      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-17T22:46:25.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹18.74 (vs ₹21.65 in FY 2025)",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹18.74 (down from ₹21.65 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹63.1b (up 17% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹3.78b (down 13% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 6.0% (down from 8.1% in FY 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue is forecast to grow 9.2% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 10% growth forecast for the Food industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 1% per year but the company’s share price has increased by 12% per year, which means it is well ahead of earnings.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "27c6b14d-4336-4471-9599-b51d76ce5c6c",
      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-05-09T19:03:52.000Z",
      "title": "BALRAMCHIN: Planned Fundraising And New Kumbhi Projects Will Support Bullish Outlook",
      "body": "Analysts have maintained their fair value estimate for Balrampur Chini Mills at about ₹616 per share, reflecting only marginal adjustments to the discount rate, revenue growth, profit margin and future P/E assumptions, rather than a material change in their overall view. What's in the News Board meeting scheduled on April 23, 2026 to consider a proposal to raise funds through issue of securities on a preferential basis, seek shareholder approval via an Extra Ordinary General Meeting, and consider limits for issuing non convertible debentures in one or more tranches in line with SEBI regulations for large corporates (Key Developments).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/food-beverage-tobacco/nse-balramchin/balrampur-chini-mills-shares/60k3y9op-government-policies-and-renewable-materials-will-shape-indias-future-uci0/updates/21-analysts-have-maintained-their-fair-value-estimate-for-balra",
